  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: df58795d0a3134c5da043aa1a759d47b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Mabel_Quest_Road
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Arlen::Arlen.DialogueSystem.DialogueData
  defaultSpeaker: Mabel
  lines:
  - speaker: You
    text: Mabel, have any traders come down the Mosswood Road lately? From the northern market?
  - speaker: 
    text: The Mosswood... road? There's no road through Mosswood, dear. Just trees, boars and that silly old signpost.
  - speaker: 
    text: Though now you mention it, Eldon asked me something just like that. The last morning I saw him.
  - speaker: 
    text: He kept staring north, muttering about "the bells going quiet". Then he bought two loaves instead of one.
  - speaker: You
    text: Two loaves. He was packing for a trip.
  - speaker: 
    text: If you go poking about in Mosswood, mind those ruffians. And you come back for supper, you hear?
